coder › Done. Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts` and added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`, committed as two commits (`eee2c15` implementation, `9f073ac` tests).

**What it does**

- Walks the document line by line, tracking whether it is inside a `` ``` `` fenced code block. A fence opens on a line with `{0,3}` leading spaces followed by 3+ backticks; inside one, only a line of 3+ backticks with nothing but trailing spaces/tabs after them, at least as long as the opening run, closes it (so `` ```` `` is not closed by `` ``` ``). An info string on the opening fence (` ```ts `) is allowed.
- Outside fences, an ATX heading is `{0,3}` leading spaces, 1–6 `#`, then whitespace (a lone `#` with no space is not a heading). `level` is the number of `#`.
- `text` is the content after the opening marks, with surrounding whitespace trimmed, and a trailing closing run of `#` marks separated by whitespace is also dropped (e.g. `## Title ##` → `Title`, while `# C#` keeps `C#`).
- `slug` lower-cases the text, collapses every run of non-letter/non-digit characters to one dash, and trims dashes from both ends. Slugs are made unique by appending `-2`, `-3`, … to any slug already used (tracked via a `Set`, so a heading `A-2` after `A`, `A` becomes `a-2-2`).

